  "description": "Subject: Deployment Specification for **myservice** (v\u202f2023\u201101\u201101\u202f12:00\u202fUTC)\n\nThe service **myservice** will run under the Unix user **appuser** and is version\u2011controlled at the timestamp\u202f2023\u201101\u201101T12:00:00Z. It is allocated 0.5\u202fCPU units, 256\u202fMiB of memory, and 10\u202fGiB of disk space, with two instances scheduled to start. The job accepts any resource role (\u201c*\u201d) and will be launched with the command `echo Hello World`; the executor field is intentionally left empty. Environment variables are limited to a single entry, **ENV_VAR=value**. A back\u2011off strategy is configured: after a failure the system will wait 10\u202fseconds before retrying, multiplying subsequent waits by a factor of\u202f1.5. No additional constraints have been defined.\n\nHealth monitoring relies on an HTTP check: the container will execute `curl -f http://localhost/health` targeting path **/health** on port index\u202f0, using the HTTP protocol. The check permits a 30\u2011second grace period, runs every 10\u202fseconds, times out after 5\u202fseconds, and tolerates up to three consecutive failures; HTTP 1xx responses are not ignored. Ports are not required to be pre\u2011allocated (`requirePorts: false`), and the service advertises port\u202f8080. The application fetches its artifact from `http://example.com/resource.tar.gz` and may also pull from the store at `http://store.example.com`.\n\nThe container is defined as type **DOCKER**, pulling the image **nginx:latest** from a Docker registry with `forcePullImage` set to true and running in **BRIDGE** network mode. It is not privileged. Docker launch parameters include `log-driver=json-file`. Port mapping translates container port\u202f80 (TCP) to a dynamically assigned host port, exposing it as service port\u202f8080. A volume mounts the host directory `/var/data` into the container at `/data` with read\u2011write mode. Labels tag the deployment with `team=devops`. Finally, the upgrade strategy specifies that at least 50\u202f% of instances must remain healthy during a rollout (`minimumHealthCapacity: 0.5`) and that no more than 20\u202f% may exceed capacity (`maximumOverCapacity: 0.2`).",
  "reference_json": {
    "id": "myservice",
    "cpus": 0.5,
    "mem": 256,
    "disk": 10,
    "instances": 2,
    "acceptedResourceRoles": [
      "*"
    ],
    "cmd": "echo Hello World",
    "backoffSeconds": 10,
    "backoffFactor": 1.5,
    "env": {
      "ENV_VAR": "value"
    },
    "executor": "",
    "healthChecks": [
      {
        "command": {
          "value": "curl -f http://localhost/health"
        },
        "gracePeriodSeconds": 30,
        "intervalSeconds": 10,
        "maxConsecutiveFailures": 3,
        "path": "/health",
        "portIndex": 0,
        "protocol": "HTTP",
        "timeoutSeconds": 5,
        "ignoreHttp1xx": false
      }
    ],
    "requirePorts": false,
    "ports": [
      8080
    ],
    "uris": [
      "http://example.com/resource.tar.gz"
    ],
    "storeUrls": [
      "http://store.example.com"
    ],
    "labels": {
      "team": "devops"
    },
    "version": "2023-01-01T12:00:00Z",
    "user": "appuser",
    "constraints": [],
    "container": {
      "type": "DOCKER",
      "docker": {
        "image": "nginx:latest",
        "network": "BRIDGE",
        "forcePullImage": true,
        "privileged": false,
        "parameters": [
          {
            "key": "log-driver",
            "value": "json-file"
          }
        ],
        "portMappings": [
          {
            "containerPort": 80,
            "hostPort": 0,
            "protocol": "tcp",
            "servicePort": 8080
          }
        ]
      },
      "volumes": [
        {
          "containerPath": "/data",
          "hostPath": "/var/data",
          "mode": "RW"
        }
      ]
    },
    "upgradeStrategy": {
      "minimumHealthCapacity": 0.5,
      "maximumOverCapacity": 0.2
    }
  }
